   "title": "Kwara Promotes 5,956 Teachers, Others",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/kwara-promotes-5956-teachers-others/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:17:08 +0000",
   "_dt": 1792775828.0,
   "ageDays": 0.02,
   "summary": "“Let me put it on record that, apart from prompt payment of monthly salaries, regular training and re-training of teachers, and approval of the implementation of 27.5% Teachers Specific Allowance(TSA), Governor AbdulRahman AbdulRazaq has consistently implemented the promotion of teachers from 2017 to date.",
   "summary_zh": "“我要明确记录在案：除了按时发放月度工资、定期对教师开展培训和再培训，以及批准落实27.5%的教师专项津贴（TSA）之外，州长AbdulRahman AbdulRazaq自2017年至今一直持续推动教师晋升。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The chairman of SUBEB, Prof. Shehu Raheem Adaramaja, disclosed this on Friday. Adaramaja said that the affected employees would have their promotion cash-backed with effect from October 2026. He directed the beneficiaries to collect their promotion letters from the Education Secretaries in their respective Local Government Areas. In October, the Board conducted a CBT promotion exercise for deserving workers, following the approval of Governor AbdulRazaq. Adaramaja said that the gesture was part of Governor AbdulRazaq’s commitment to boosting the morale of the workforce and improving service delivery. “Let me put it on record that, apart from prompt payment of monthly salaries, regular training and re-training of teachers, and approval of the implementation of 27.5% Teachers Specific Allowance(TSA), Governor AbdulRahman AbdulRazaq has consistently implemented the promotion of teachers from 2017 to date. “This includes the arrears of SUBEB staff promotions inherited from the previous administration. The Governor has long settled 345% of salary arrears accrued from instalment payments inherited from the past administration. “The government is taking every step within available resources to drive efficient performance of students in public basic schools. This is partly achievable when their teachers are well taken care of,” Adaramaja added. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates → Join Our WhatsApp Channel --> --> Abdullahi Olesin Abdullahi Olesin is an award‑winning journalist with roughly three decades of experience. He currently reports for LEADERSHIP Newspaper. Over the years, his reporting has contributed to development and peaceful coexistence in Nigeria. He can be reached via [email protected]",
