   "ageDays": 0.03,
   "summary": "Unlock these with Subscription Several people are feared dead after a blast in a firecracker factory in Bihar’ Siwan district on Friday (October 23, 2026). Preliminary reports said that two dead bodies have been recovered so far from the blast site, though, several others too might have been killed in the severe blast, a district police official on condition of anonymity said. Amaruddin Mian, at whose house firecrackers manufacturing has been going on for several years.",
   "summary_zh": "订阅后解锁。据信周五（2026年10月23日），比哈尔邦锡万县一家鞭炮厂发生爆炸，多人恐已死亡。初步报告显示，迄今已从爆炸现场找到两具遗体；一名要求匿名的县警官员表示，强烈爆炸可能还造成多人死亡。Amaruddin Mian 的家中多年来一直从事鞭炮生产。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Account subscription benefits alongside Premium Stories, Editorials, Opinions and more. Unlock these with Subscription Several people are feared dead after a blast in a firecracker factory in Bihar’ Siwan district on Friday (October 23, 2026). Preliminary reports said that two dead bodies have been recovered so far from the blast site, though, several others too might have been killed in the severe blast, a district police official on condition of anonymity said. Rescue operations are under way under town Sub-Divisional Officer (SDO) Ashutish Kumar Gupta, while top police officials reached the blast site. The workers were said to be making firecrackers for the upcoming Deepavali festival at the factory in Almapur village under Jamo police station. According to locals, the blast occurred at the residence of Mohd. Amaruddin Mian, at whose house firecrackers manufacturing has been going on for several years. Family members of Mr. Amaruddin Mian are also said to have been killed in the blast, though, official confirmation is still awaited. Comments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our community guidelines for posting your comments. We have migrated to a new commenting platform. If you are already a registered user of The Hindu and logged in, you may continue to engage with our articles. If you do not have an account please register and login to post comments. Users can access their older comments by logging into their accounts on Vuukle",
