   "title": "US envoy highlights shipbuilding cooperation with S. Korea",
   "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/world/20261023/us-envoy-highlights-shipbuilding-cooperation-with-s-korea",
   "domain": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "source": "koreatimes.co.kr",
   "published": "Fri, 23 Oct 2026 14:32:03 GMT",
   "_dt": 1792765923.0,
   "ageDays": 0.14,
   "summary": "WASHINGTON — U.S. Ambassador to South Korea Michelle Steel on Thursday highlighted the potential for greater shipbuilding cooperation between Seoul and Washington following a visit to a shipyard operated by Samsung Heavy Industries Co. \"By combining American and Korean expertise, we can strengthen our shipbuilding industries, drive innovation and create new opportunities for workers in both countries,\" she wrote in a post on social media platform X after visiting the Geoje shipyard, about 330 kilometers south of Seoul.",
   "summary_zh": "华盛顿——美国驻韩国大使Michelle Steel于周四强调，首尔和华盛顿有望在参观Samsung Heavy Industries Co.运营的船厂后，进一步加强造船合作。她在社交媒体平台X发文称，参观位于首尔以南约330公里的巨济船厂后，她写道：“融合美国和韩国的专业知识，我们可以增强双方造船产业、推动创新，并为两国工人创造新的机会。”",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "WASHINGTON — U.S. Ambassador to South Korea Michelle Steel on Thursday highlighted the potential for greater shipbuilding cooperation between Seoul and Washington following a visit to a shipyard operated by Samsung Heavy Industries Co. \"By combining American and Korean expertise, we can strengthen our shipbuilding industries, drive innovation and create new opportunities for workers in both countries,\" she wrote in a post on social media platform X after visiting the Geoje shipyard, about 330 kilometers south of Seoul. She thanked Samsung Heavy Industries, the world's fifth-largest shipbuilder in terms of its existing orders, for welcoming her and for sharing the company's vision for shipbuilding cooperation. The remarks come amid South Korea's broader efforts to revive the U.S. shipbuilding industry under the MASGA, or \"Make American Shipbuilding Great Again,\" initiative. Earlier this year, Samsung Heavy Industries established a research center in San Diego to support the South Korea-U.S. initiative. The SHI-SDSU Advanced Maritime Center, jointly launched with San Diego State University, was established to explore cooperation to support the revitalization of the U.S. shipbuilding industry in areas such as artificial intelligence (AI)-based production automation, robotics and eco-friendly technologies, according to the company",
