   "ageDays": 1.14,
   "summary": "The Korean won strengthened against the U.S. dollar Thursday, after the Bank of Korea (BOK) left its key rate unchanged, but hinted at further tightening. The won was quoted at 1,324.2 won per dollar at 3:30 p.m., up 1 won from the close of the previous stock trading session. BOK Gov. Shin Hyun-song told reporters that the won \"is still undervalued in terms of effective exchange rate.\" The won has appreciated to around 1,320 won per U.S. dollar from around 1,560 won in June",
   "summary_zh": "韩国银行（央行）周四维持基准利率不变，但暗示将进一步收紧货币政策，此后韩元对美元汇率走强。当日下午3时30分，韩元兑美元报1324.2韩元兑1美元，较前一交易日股市收盘时升值1韩元。韩国银行行长申炫松（音）告诉记者，韩元\"按实际有效汇率衡量仍被低估\"。韩元汇率已从6月份的约1560韩元兑1美元升至目前的约1320韩元兑1美元。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "The Korean won strengthened against the U.S. dollar Thursday, after the Bank of Korea (BOK) left its key rate unchanged, but hinted at further tightening. The won was quoted at 1,324.2 won per dollar at 3:30 p.m., up 1 won from the close of the previous stock trading session. For a fifth consecutive session, the won marked the highest level since Oct. 2, 2024. In a widely expected decision, the BOK held the key rate steady at 3 percent in its rate-setting meeting earlier in the day. BOK Gov. Shin Hyun-song told reporters that the won \"is still undervalued in terms of effective exchange rate.\" The won has appreciated to around 1,320 won per U.S. dollar from around 1,560 won in June",
