   "title": "Presidency Expands Skills Acquisition Programmes To Tackle Insecurity",
   "url": "https://leadership.ng/presidency-expands-skills-acquisition-programmes-to-tackle-insecurity/",
   "domain": "leadership.ng",
   "source": "Leadership（尼日利亚）",
   "published": "Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:05:40 +0000",
   "_dt": 1792613140.0,
   "ageDays": 1.91,
   "summary": "Both presidential aides recognised the need for a comprehensive security approach combining military and law enforcement operations with education, skills development and economic inclusion, particularly for vulnerable youths. Famadewa stressed the need for a holistic approach to insecurity that incorporates non-kinetic measures and addresses its underlying socioeconomic drivers.",
   "summary_zh": "两位总统助手都认识到需要采取全面的安全方法，将军事和执法行动与教育、技能发展和经济包容结合起来，特别是针对弱势青年。法马德瓦强调需要采取整体方法应对不安全问题，纳入非军事手段并解决其潜在的社会经济驱动因素。",
   "summarySource": "fulltext",
   "body": "Senior Special Assistant to President Bola Tinubu on Technical, Vocational and Entrepreneurship Education (TVEE), Dr Abiola Arogundade disclosed this on Wednesday in Abuja during a meeting with Maj.-Gen. Adeyinka A. Famadewa (Rtd), Special Adviser to the President on Homeland Security, at her office. The meeting explored areas of collaboration between the two offices, focusing on economic empowerment, employability and sustainable livelihoods as complementary measures to conventional security operations. Arogundade said the partnership seeks to empower citizens, expand awareness and create sustainable opportunities for positive engagement. “This partnership seeks to strengthen cooperation between both offices in empowering our people, broadening their awareness, and creating sustainable opportunities for their positive engagement. “Through these collective efforts, we aim to steer them away from crime and criminality while fostering a safer, more enlightened, and empowered society,” she said. Both presidential aides recognised the need for a comprehensive security approach combining military and law enforcement operations with education, skills development and economic inclusion, particularly for vulnerable youths. Under the proposed collaboration, the TVEE would seek to reduce the vulnerability of unemployed and economically disadvantaged youths to recruitment by criminal networks exploiting poverty, limited opportunities and social exclusion. By linking vocational education with homeland security objectives, the partnership is expected to strengthen community resilience, promote social stability and support individuals seeking alternatives to criminal activities. Famadewa stressed the need for a holistic approach to insecurity that incorporates non-kinetic measures and addresses its underlying socioeconomic drivers. His office is also focused on unified intelligence and surveillance, stronger border security, improved identification of security threats, and effective protocols for reporting and responding to crises. The proposed collaboration reflects President Bola Ahmed Tinubu’s administration’s efforts to link education, economic opportunities, and national security. By promoting skills development and supporting entrepreneurship, the initiative aims to create pathways to sustainable livelihoods, strengthen peacebuilding efforts and foster long-term stability. We’ve got the edge. Get real-time reports, breaking scoops, and exclusive angles delivered straight to your phone. Don’t settle for stale news. Join LEADERSHIP NEWS on WhatsApp for 24/7 updates →",
