   "snippet": "Africa Corps under pressure: the 🌴Sahel, April–October 2026\n\nRussia promised security to the Sahel’s military regimes. The facts tell a different story.\n\n🇲🇱 Mali: On 25 April, coordinated 🥷JNIM and FLA attacks struck several locations, including Bamako and Kati. Defence Minister Sadio Camara was killed and Kidal fell to the FLA. On 10 September, JNIM overran Dioura, reportedly killing over 100 Malian soldiers and five Africa Corps personnel. Russian-backed forces returned to Kidal in October after the FLA withdrew—but holding it remains the real test.\n\n🇧🇫 Burkina Faso: JNIM continues to inflict heavy losses. At least 34 civilians were reportedly executed in Titao in February; around 90 soldiers were reportedly killed in a September ambush at Koubel-Alpha.\n\n🇳🇪 Niger: More than 50 security personnel were reportedly killed in two September attacks. Even Niamey’s military infrastructure has been targeted. Africa Corps has not stopped the insurgency.\n\nThe verdict: Russia’s presence has not delivered security. The 🇺🇸US State Department advises Americans NOT TO TRAVEL to all three AES countries.\n\n#AES #Sahel #Mali #BurkinaFaso #Niger #JNIM",
