   "platform": "x",
   "title": "Obasanjo is only repeating the obvious here.",
   "url": "https://x.com/realYusufTukur/status/2113233057364738346",
   "snippet": "Obasanjo is only repeating the obvious here.\n\nAll sensible people knew that Bola @officialABAT’s gross incompetence triggered the Sahel Nations out of ECOWAS.\nHe wanted to prove his renewed subservience to President Macron of France 🇫🇷 , so he naively sanctioned Niger Republic 🇳🇪 and threatened to invade the country unless the toppled President Bazoum was reinstated within an ultimatum.\n\nBut Niger is a country that doesn’t take external threats lightly. In 2009 when President Tandja Mamadou organised and won a referendum for tenure extension, Niger was suspended from the ECOWAS. The Nigerien officials responded strongly, reminding ECOWAS that countries make up the block, not the other way round, and threatened to leave if the interference in their internal affairs continued.\n\nThe only thing that stopped adamant Niger’s breakaway then was possibly the military coup led by Salou Djibo in early 2010. Nigeria was happy with the coup then, as it was even alleged that General Abdulsalam Abubakar, who led ECOWAS delegation to the country in 2009, effectively planned the coup during his mission in Niger.\n\nFast forwarded to 2023, similar scenario played out in Niger 🇳🇪, where Soldiers led by Abdourahamane Tciani overthrew President Mohamed Bazoum after serving just 2 years of his 5-year mandate.\n\nBut this time around, Nigeria is unhappy with the coup. So, Bola and his inept advisers who lack knowledge of history and international affairs or willingly ignored both to carry out the command of their “slavemaster” France, whose interests are threatened by Bazoum’s removal, responded with an unprecedentedly disdainful and hostile threat against the Nigerien Junta.\n\nIf civilian officials of Niger strongly rejected much lesser threats in 2009, what would anyone expect of their Military, 14 years later?\n\nNiger is a good neighbour and a key stakeholder in the Multinational Joint Task Force (MNJTF) that helps in the fight against terrorism affecting our country and the broader Sahel region. They help us with intelligence and even live data about terrorists movements. Above all, they helped us in the Civil War and played a significant role in keeping Nigeria as one country which Bola now enjoys to govern.\n\nBut all that did not matter to Bola and his disastrous regime.\n\nAll he and his failed NSA Nuhu @NuhuRibadu (aka DPO) care about is politics rather than protecting the lives and properties of citizens, then claiming credit for a “rescue” by ONSA (or is it ONGA)’s “tactical team” after citizens have paid ransom to get their loved ones released.\n\nOya, let the blockheaded BATidiots start abusing Obasanjo. They’ve been hailing him on remarks against Atiku.",
   "body": "Obasanjo is only repeating the obvious here.\n\nAll sensible people knew that Bola @officialABAT’s gross incompetence triggered the Sahel Nations out of ECOWAS.\nHe wanted to prove his renewed subservience to President Macron of France 🇫🇷 , so he naively sanctioned Niger Republic 🇳🇪 and threatened to invade the country unless the toppled President Bazoum was reinstated within an ultimatum.\n\nBut Niger is a country that doesn’t take external threats lightly. In 2009 when President Tandja Mamadou organised and won a referendum for tenure extension, Niger was suspended from the ECOWAS. The Nigerien officials responded strongly, reminding ECOWAS that countries make up the block, not the other way round, and threatened to leave if the interference in their internal affairs continued.\n\nThe only thing that stopped adamant Niger’s breakaway then was possibly the military coup led by Salou Djibo in early 2010. Nigeria was happy with the coup then, as it was even alleged that General Abdulsalam Abubakar, who led ECOWAS delegation to the country in 2009, effectively planned the coup during his mission in Niger.\n\nFast forwarded to 2023, similar scenario played out in Niger 🇳🇪, where Soldiers led by Abdourahamane Tciani overthrew President Mohamed Bazoum after serving just 2 years of his 5-year mandate.\n\nBut this time around, Nigeria is unhappy with the coup. So, Bola and his inept advisers who lack knowledge of history and international affairs or willingly ignored both to carry out the command of their “slavemaster” France, whose interests are threatened by Bazoum’s removal, responded with an unprecedentedly disdainful and hostile threat against the Nigerien Junta.\n\nIf civilian officials of Niger strongly rejected much lesser threats in 2009, what would anyone expect of their Military, 14 years later?\n\nNiger is a good neighbour and a key stakeholder in the Multinational Joint Task Force (MNJTF) that helps in the fight against terrorism affecting our country and the broader Sahel region. They help us with intelligence and even live data about terrorists movements. Above all, they helped us in the Civil War and played a significant role in keeping Nigeria as one country which Bola now enjoys to govern.\n\nBut all that did not matter to Bola and his disastrous regime.\n\nAll he and his failed NSA Nuhu @NuhuRibadu (aka DPO) care about is politics rather than protecting the lives and properties of citizens, then claiming credit for a “rescue” by ONSA (or is it ONGA)’s “tactical team” after citizens have paid ransom to get their loved ones released.\n\nOya, let the blockheaded BATidiots start abusing Obasanjo. They’ve been hailing him on remarks against Atiku.",
