   "snippet": "The Sahel’s terrorism epicenter is the Mali-Burkina Faso-Niger tri-border (Liptako-Gourma). Per AFRICOM and Global Terrorism Index data, it drives over half of worldwide terror deaths. JNIM (al-Qaeda affiliate, 7-8k fighters) dominates with expansions, blockades, and attacks into coastal states and mining areas. Rival ISSP (IS, ~2k fighters) contests it fiercely—recent Oct 2026 clashes claimed 400+ dead. After Western exits, AES juntas rely on Russian Africa Corps; groups exploit weak governance and local grievances, sustaining high violence and spillover risks.",
